PT Image 2 prompting guide\n\nImage\n\nImage: Codex for (almost) everything\n\n### Codex for (almost) everything\n\nApril 16, 2026\n\nRealtime and audio Codex changelog Community page\n\n## Blog posts\n\nView all\n\nMaking private MCP servers reachable without making them public How we preserved private network boundaries while supporting MCP streaming, authentication, and an inspectable client. Jun 26, 2026 General Mastering remote engineering work from your phone Use Remote in the ChatGPT mobile app to start, steer, review, and organize engineering work. Jun 23, 2026 Codex Using skills to accelerate OSS maintenance Using skills and GitHub Actions to optimize Codex workflows in the OpenAI Agents SDK repos. Mar 9, 2026 Codex\n\n## Cookbooks\n\nView all\n\nBuilding workspace agents in ChatGPT to complete repeatable, end-to-end work ChatGPTSecurityMigrate a Legacy Codebase with Sandbox Agents Agents SDKEvalsSecurityContext Engineering for Personalization - State Management with Long-Term Memory Notes Agents SDK\n\nHelp center Frequently asked account and billing questions Developer forum Discuss topics with other developers OpenAI Academy Courses and resources for learning about AI Status Check the status of OpenAI services\n\nAsk AI\n\n## Docs agent\n\nLoading docs agent...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommunity | OpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/community)\nciteturn8search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Join a global community of developers building with OpenAI. ... Find the right place to connect, contribute, get support, or grow with the OpenAI developer community. ... given the interest, I productized my video hub! - have 1 place for video drafts + X, Youtube, tiktok vids - use the studio to comment + collab with others - get transcripts + add API keys for autosyncs/agent chat made with codex 5.3 🖤 linked below ... The Codex app feels like the missing IDE layer for the Codex CLI.\n### Angel ❄️\n\n@Angaisb_\n\nGPT-5.3 Codex is actually pretty insane with Three.js This Minecraft clone works smoothly and it didn't take too long to make I also tried Opus 4.6, but for some reason it got stuck\n\nFeb 5, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Angel ❄️\n\n@Angaisb_\n\nGPT-5.3-Codex with image gen skill (NBP) I'm loving this model so much. This is one-shot\n\nVideo\n\nFeb 5, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Flavio Adamo\n\n@flavioAd\n\nCodex app is the most 'non-native' app that somehow feels more native than native apps\n\nImage\n\nFeb 2, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Pallav Agarwal\n\n@pallavmac\n\nOk the new Codex app is incredible. You can build and run an Xcode project from Codex directly so you can vibecode iOS apps without opening Xcode!\n\nFeb 2, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Paul Solt\n\n@PaulSolt\n\nThe Codex app feels like the missing IDE layer for the Codex CLI. One-click to open Xcode, run iOS/macOS apps, review diffs, and manage agents. Hard to go back after this.\n\nFeb 2, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Kristen Anderson\nCost $4.14 and 45 minutes.\n\nMar 5, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Mitchell Hashimoto\n\n@mitchellh\n\nI know this is pretty well established at this point, but Codex 5.3 is a much more effective model than Opus 4.6. I went back and forth on both for a bit, but haven't touched Opus at all now for a full week. First model to get me off of Opus... ever. Good job Codex team.\n\nFeb 25, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Dennis Hannusch\n\n@DennisHannusch\n\nI started daily driving Codex with gpt-5.3-codex this week.. it's reaaally good. I've gotten used to complex workflows and context management, but Codex just does what I ask. I keep expecting quality to drop deep into a session, but it doesn't. @OpenAIDevs ya'll cooked!\n\nFeb 11, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Christopher Ehrlich\n\n@ccccjjjjeeee\n\nIt actually worked! For the past couple of days I've been throwing 5.3-codex at the C codebase for SimCity (1989) to port it to TypeScript. Not reading any code, very little steering. Today I have SimCity running in the browser. I can't believe this new world we live in.\n\nImage\n\nFeb 10, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Guillermo Rauch\n\n@rauchg\n\n🆕 GPT 5.3 Codex (xhigh) achieves 90% on Next.js evals out of the box, \"frame-mogging\" the competition so to speak:\n\nImage\n\nFeb 9, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Flavio Adamo\n\n@flavioAd\n\nCodex app is the most 'non-native' app that somehow feels more native than native apps\n\nImage\n\nFeb 2, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Paul Solt\n\n@PaulSolt\n\nThe Codex app feels like the missing IDE layer for the Codex CLI. One-click to open Xcode, run iOS/macOS apps, review diffs, and manage agents. Hard to go back after this.\n\nFeb 2, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Dennis Hannusch\n\n@DennisHannusch\n\nI started daily driving Codex with gpt-5.3-codex this week.. it's reaaally good. I've gotten used to complex workflows and context management, but Codex just does what I ask. I keep expecting quality to drop deep into a session, but it doesn't. @OpenAIDevs ya'll cooked!\n\nFeb 11, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Dan Shipper 📧\n\n@danshipper\n\nBREAKING: At the Super Bowl halftime show, Bad Bunny says he prefers Opus 4.6 for vibe coding but turns to 5.3 Codex for gnarly engineering problems. \"Opus pa'' vibear, Codex pa'' lo heavy\" - he said\n\nFeb 9, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Angel ❄️\n\n@Angaisb_\n\nGPT-5.3-Codex with image gen skill (NBP) I'm loving this model so much. This is one-shot\n\nVideo\n\nFeb 5, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Paul Solt\n\n@PaulSolt\n\nThe Codex app feels like the missing IDE layer for the Codex CLI. One-click to open Xcode, run iOS/macOS apps, review diffs, and manage agents. Hard to go back after this.\n\nFeb 2, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Anthony\n\n@kr0der\n\nCodex v0.91.0 has plan mode, and it's really thorough. this one plan took 27% of its context. if you've used Codex you know that 27% is a lot which means it's thoroughly searching before creating plans - no rushing/taking shortcuts. try it out by adding 'collaboration_modes =…\n------------------------------------------------